meta {
  name: Delete asset
  type: http
  seq: 8
}

delete {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/media/assets/{{assetId}}
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 204
}

docs {
  # Delete asset

  `DELETE /api/media/assets/{{assetId}}`

  Delete the primary cloud file, optional thumbnail, and asset record.

  ## Authentication

  Admin or Editor; inherited Bearer token.

  ## Parameters

  | Name | Location | Meaning |
  | --- | --- | --- |
  | assetId | Path | GUID; replace the example with a real resource. |

  ## Request body

  No request body.

  ## Response

  HTTP **204**.

  Empty response body.

  ## Errors

  - 404: Asset not found.
  - 500: unhandled storage/database failure.
  - 401: missing, invalid, or expired Bearer token.
  - 403: authenticated token with an insufficient role.

  Automatic model validation can return ValidationProblemDetails; explicit controller errors use a message field. Authentication middleware errors may have no body.

  ## Notes

  No body. May leave a post without assets. Storage and database deletion are not one transaction; partial deletion is possible.

  Examples contain fictitious data. The assertion checks the successful scenario; a missing record or insufficient permissions can produce a different documented status.
}
